    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/Dutton-Park/Postdoctoral-Research-Fellow_R-67967-1": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Fellow",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nFrazer Institute Full-time, fixed-term position until December 2027 Base salary will be in the range $85,372 - $113,659 + 17% super (Academic Level A)  Based at the Translational Research Institute at our Dutton Park Campus About This Opportunity    Join a visionary and highly collaborative research team at the forefront of cancer epigenomics and precision medicine. Based within UQ’s renowned Frazer Institute and Translational Research Institute, this exciting Postdoctoral Research Fellow opportunity will contribute to a major international research program funded by the US Department of Defense, focused on understanding and overcoming therapeutic resistance in uveal melanoma. Working alongside leading researchers, partner universities, and industry collaborators, you will leverage cutting-edge bioinformatics, AI, machine learning, and multi-omics technologies to drive discoveries that have the potential to transform cancer diagnosis, treatment, and patient outcomes. This is an exceptional opportunity to create meaningful impact while building your research profile within a world-class, purpose-driven environment dedicated to creating change together  Key responsibilities will include :    Research:  Lead innovative bioinformatics research focused on cancer epigenomics, gene expression, single-cell and spatial omics, and metabolomic data analysis. Develop computational tools, apply AI and machine learning approaches to identify novel biomarkers and therapeutic targets, contribute to competitive research funding applications, publish in high-impact journals, and collaborate with national and international research partners. Supervision and Researcher Development:  Contribute to the supervision and mentoring of Honours and Higher Degree by Research students, support researcher development through coaching and feedback, foster a collaborative research culture, and assist in the effective management and development of research support staff where required. Citizenship and Service:  Demonstrate leadership through collaboration and active participation in institute and university initiatives, contribute to committees and administrative activities, support colleagues and unit operations, build partnerships with industry, government and research stakeholders, and uphold UQ values through professional and inclusive engagement. This is a  research focused  position. Further information can be found by viewing UQ’s  Criteria for Academic Performance .      About You    Completion, or near completion, of a PhD in Bioinformatics, Data Science, Computational Biology, Immunology, or a related discipline. Demonstrated expertise in bioinformatics, statistical analysis, and computational methods for analysing complex biological datasets. Experience with single-cell and spatial omics technologies, including transcriptomics, metabolomics, or multi-omics data integration. Proficiency in programming languages and analytical tools such as R, Python, and machine learning frameworks. A strong track record of research outputs, including publications in high-quality peer-reviewed journals and conference presentations. Excellent interpersonal, communication, analytical, and project management skills, with the ability to work both independently and collaboratively in multidisciplinary research teams. About the Frazer Institute, UQ, TRI The Frazer Institute at the University of Queensland is a leading research centre focusing on cancer, immunology, and the genetic basis of disease. It is best known for the development by Prof Ian Frazer AC of the Gardasil cervical cancer vaccine which has saved thousands of lives. As part of the Faculty of Medicine, the Frazer Institute is situated in the Translational Research Institute (TRI) at the Princess Alexandra Hospital site in Woolloongabba, which is linked to the St Lucia and Herston UQ campuses by an easy bus ride. TRI provides world-class research facilities for commercialisation and the translation of scientific discoveries to the clinic.  The greater  benefits  of joining the UQ community are broad: from being part of a  Group of Eight  university, to recognition of prior service with other Australian universities, up to 26 weeks of paid parental leave, 17.5% annual leave loading, flexible working arrangements, access to exclusive internal-only vacancies, and genuine career progression opportunities via the academic promotions process.   Interested?   For more information about this opportunity, please contact Associate Professor Jason Lee at jason.s.lee@uq.edu.au For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at  talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number (below) in the subject line.   When you apply, please ensure you upload a  resume ,  cover letter , and  responses to the ‘About You’ section.       Other Information    Pre-employment checks may include verification of the right to work in Australia, qualifications, criminal history checks and mandatory immunisations. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements.   Relocating from interstate or overseas? We may support you with obtaining employer-sponsored work rights and a relocation support package, however upfront costs will still be expected to be covered. You can find out more about life in  Australia’s Sunshine State here .   We're dedicated to  equity, diversity, and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ, and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criteria but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing  talent@uq.edu.au  or calling +61 7 3365 2623.  Applications close Friday the 25th of September 2026 at 11.00pm AEST (R-67967)."
    },
    "https://uq.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/uqcareers/job/Gatton-Campus/Veterinary-Nurse---Equine_R-68030-1": {
      "title": "Veterinary Nurse - Equine",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nUQ VETS . Full-time (100%), fixed-term position through to 4 September 2027. Base salary will be in the range $79,096 to $83,863 + 17% super (HEW Level 4). Join our Gatton Campus community and take a virtual tour . About This Opportunity Join the collaborative team at the UQ VETS Equine Specialist Hospital, where you will provide high-quality nursing and technical services for hospitalised equine patients while supporting the clinical education of veterinary and veterinary technology students. Working alongside veterinarians, veterinary specialists and support colleagues in an advanced clinical environment, you will contribute to exceptional patient care and help create meaningful change for animals, clients and the next generation of veterinary professionals. As a Day-Position role within our 24-hour facility, you will be exposed to a broad range of cases and have opportunities to develop your skills across multiple specialty areas. Your take-home salary will reflect the specific terms of your roster. Key responsibilities will include, but not limited to: Assess, monitor and treat equine patients in intensive care, isolation and hospital wards, while maintaining excellent standards of husbandry and professional nursing care. Provide skilled technical assistance to veterinary specialists and staff, including support for radiography, computed tomography, scintigraphy, magnetic resonance imaging and relevant diagnostic clinical pathology procedures. Maintain specialised instruments and equipment, assist with pharmacy inventory, and deliver responsive administrative, reception and client service support. Provide clinical training and teaching support for veterinary and veterinary technology students, while liaising confidently with veterinarians, specialists, colleagues and clients about patient treatment and care. About UQ VETS A career at UQ VETS means making a difference to not only the lives of the people and animals in your care, but also the next generation of vets and vet technicians. At UQ VETS, we offer the opportunity to build a dynamic career through structured development programs and access to industry leaders. Instead of solely concentrating on meeting caseload benchmarks or revenue targets, your priorities lie in creating an impact, establishing a lasting impression on the field, and conducting work that brings about positive changes in the lives of animals. The Veterinary Teaching Hospital is an organisational unit within the School that includes all of the School’s outstanding clinical facilities. UQ VETS Equine Hospital is a largely referral-based hospital with advanced facilities and offers a 24-hour emergency medical and surgical service. UQ VETS Small Animal Hospital boasts the latest veterinary medical and surgical diagnostic and treatment options for small animals, birds, exotic pets and wildlife, as well as a seven-day urgent and emergency care service. UQ staff also supervise clinical placements at the RSPCA’s Brisbane Animal Care Campus, Wacol. In particular, the UQ VETS Equine Specialist Hospital brings world-leading specialist veterinarians and nurses together to provide outstanding veterinary care for horses. We are proud of the service we deliver and strive to provide horse owners and trainers with the best available treatment options and outcomes for their horses. You can also take a virtual tour of UQ’s Gatton facilities . About UQ As part of the UQ community, you’ll have the opportunity to work alongside the brightest minds, who have joined us from all over the world, working together to create a better world. Join a purposeful, inclusive and collaborative community where excellence is at the core of our culture, contributions are valued and a range of benefits and rewards are available, such as: Free parking and an intercampus bus . On-campus childcare , a medical clinic and a post office. Up to 26 weeks of paid parental leave or paid primary care leave. 17% super contributions and 17.5% annual leave loading. Health and wellness discounts, including Fitness Passport access, free yearly flu vaccinations, discounted health insurance and access to our Employee Assistance Program for staff and their immediate family. Career development opportunities, including access to exclusive internal-only vacancies and our Study for Staff program. A 25% discount on eligible UQ VETS services . Access to our $4.1 million UQ Sport facility . UQ’s commitment to advancing animal health is reflected in research that broadens understanding of viruses affecting people and animals. Read about UQ researchers’ identification of the first henipavirus detected in North America and their work to identify better ways to protect against this virus family . About You A Bachelor of Veterinary Technology, Bachelor of Applied Science in Veterinary Technology, Certificate IV in Veterinary Nursing or an equivalent qualification, together with relevant nursing experience. Demonstrated experience working reliably as part of a rostered team delivering equine specialist hospital services seven days a week. Demonstrated ability to provide and maintain high standards of professional veterinary nursing and equine patient care. Strong organisational skills, with the ability to work flexibly, exercise initiative and operate with appropriate autonomy. Effective written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to build productive professional and operational relationships with colleagues, clients and students. Knowledge of the ethical requirements, principles, policies and procedures relevant to veterinary nursing, including workplace health and safety, equity and anti-discrimination obligations. A collaborative approach, enthusiasm for ongoing professional development and an interest in supporting the clinical education of veterinary and veterinary technology students. A current radiation licence, or the ability to apply for one. Interested? For more information about this opportunity, please contact Sophie Alonso. For application inquiries, please reach out to the Talent Acquisition team at talent@uq.edu.au , stating the job reference number below in the subject line. When you apply, please ensure you upload a resume and cover letter summarising how your background aligns with the ‘About You’ section. Please note that applications received via email will not be accepted. Other Information Pre-employment checks may include verification of the right to work in Australia, qualifications, professional registration, criminal history checks, mandatory immunisations, First Aid and/or CPR certification, and Blue Card checks. This may also include checks relating to gender-based violence matters or other integrity and conduct requirements. You must have unrestricted work rights in Australia for the duration of this appointment to apply. Visa sponsorship is not available for this appointment. It is a condition of employment for this role that you provide evidence of immunisation against certain vaccine-preventable diseases. We’re dedicated to equity, diversity and inclusion . We recognise that career pathways and opportunities differ and encourage applications from candidates who may not meet every criterion but can demonstrate their potential relative to opportunity. We’re also happy to support any accessibility needs throughout the recruitment process. Just let us know how we can help by emailing talent@uq.edu.au or calling +61 7 3365 2623. Applications close Sunday 20 September at 11.00pm AEST (R-68030)."
    },
